provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Rename the `watched` field of watchlist items to `seen` everywhere.

governor turn 1: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist, movie-detail, search, app  (Data-field rename on WatchItem, the watchlist-item type: movie re-declares the field as `seen`; watchlist-store creates/toggles/persists it; watchlist renders it; movie-detail/search/app get a conditional scan because plain tsc does not type-check Angular templates (a stale template reference would break silently). Non-field names (toggleWatched, watchedCount, CSS classes, UI text) keep `watched` since the request targets the item field only — say so if you want those renamed too. The store also migrates legacy persisted `watched` flags so saved data survives. Existing tests pinning the old field name will surface as change requests; I will approve them next round.)
round 1: owners movie=ok watchlist-store=ok watchlist=rejected movie-detail=ok search=ok app=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> movie, watchlist-store, watchlist  (Round 1 landed the WatchItem rename (movie.ts now exports `seen`) and the store implementation. The remaining red involves exactly three units: watchlist's submission was rejected only because it updated an existing test's `.watched` assertion — that change is required by the rename and is now approved; movie's own spec still reads `.watched` and lost its `withOptionalFields` helper; watchlist-store's own spec dot-accesses an index-signature type (TS4111). No interface changes are needed this round; I re-supply my existing acceptance tests unchanged.)
round 2: owners movie=fail watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> movie  (The oracle shows only two errors left, both in src/app/movie.spec.ts (the movie owner failed with max_tokens last round, so nothing was applied). All other units compiled; target only movie with a concise, minimal instruction.)
round 3: owners movie=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 4 failed: prompt of ~32384 tokens exceeds the 12000-token budget

